# What never reaches the build context.
#
# `.env*` first and for its own reason: the image is pushed to a
# registry and the runner's four secrets are handed to it by the
# platform at run time. A .env file that got copied in would sit in a
# layer, readable by anyone who can pull the image, and would keep
# working after the key was rotated.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

node_modules
.next
.git
.gitignore
.vercel

# Everything the worker's graph does not reach. Listed rather than left
# out, because the Dockerfile copies named directories and a reader
# should be able to see that the omissions are deliberate: the worker
# renders nothing (components, hooks, public), builds no templates
# (sandbox — that is a local step against the E2B API), and runs no
# tests or benchmarks of its own.
components
hooks
public
sandbox
tests
bench
scripts
supabase
scratchpad
*.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
